              Their sleep pattern comes from their natural instinct to conserve energy between short bursts
              of activity, play, and hunting behavior.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="trigger" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
          <span class="question">What does it mean when a cat kneads?</span>
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" hidden>
          <div class="details-inner">
            <p class="answer">
              Kneading is usually a comfort behavior that starts in kittenhood. Adult cats may knead soft
              blankets, beds, or their favorite people when they feel calm, safe, and attached to their
              environment.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="trigger" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
          <span class="question">Do cats need regular playtime?</span>
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" hidden>
          <div class="details-inner">
            <p class="answer">
              Yes. Daily play supports exercise, mental stimulation, and stress relief. Short sessions with
              wand toys, balls, or puzzle feeders help indoor cats stay healthy and reduce boredom-related
              behaviors like scratching furniture or nighttime zoomies.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="trigger" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
          <span class="question">Why do cats flick or swish their tails?</span>
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" hidden>
          <div class="details-inner">
            <p class="answer">
              Tail movement can signal mood. A softly raised tail often means a cat feels friendly or
              confident, while a fast flick or strong swish can suggest overstimulation, irritation, or
              intense focus on something nearby.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <script>
    const items = document.querySelectorAll(".example");

    items.forEach((item) => {
      const trigger = item.querySelector(".trigger");
      const details = item.querySelector(".details");

      trigger.addEventListener("click", () => {
        const isOpen = item.classList.toggle("is-open");
        trigger.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(isOpen));
        details.hidden = !isOpen;
      });
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
